1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,211
A ladder leaning on a wall.

2
00:00:02,211 --> 00:00:04,249
A kite string pulled at a slant.

3
00:00:04,249 --> 00:00:05,696
A ramp up to a door.

4
00:00:06,096 --> 00:00:10,092
Each is a slanted line,
secretly doing two jobs at once.

5
00:00:10,542 --> 00:00:13,419
Aarav crosses the college
ground in two legs.

6
00:00:13,419 --> 00:00:16,681
Twenty metres one way, then
fifteen metres another.

7
00:00:17,031 --> 00:00:20,167
His friend asks: how far
from the start is he now?

8
00:00:20,167 --> 00:00:21,633
And in which direction?

9
00:00:22,083 --> 00:00:23,978
Drawing it to scale is slow.

10
00:00:23,978 --> 00:00:26,344
Components give the answer in seconds.

11
00:00:26,844 --> 00:00:28,452
First, a quick reminder.

12
00:00:28,802 --> 00:00:34,059
Any vector A has a shadow on the x
axis, A x, and a shadow on the y axis,

13
00:00:34,059 --> 00:00:34,959
A y.

14
00:00:35,042 --> 00:00:38,015
So A equals A x i hat plus A y j hat.

15
00:00:38,015 --> 00:00:41,146
One slanted arrow becomes
two straight arrows.

16
00:00:41,746 --> 00:00:43,606
Now the big idea, live.

17
00:00:43,606 --> 00:00:47,585
Aarav's first leg, A, is twenty
metres at thirty degrees.

18
00:00:47,935 --> 00:00:51,451
Its parts: A x is seventeen
point three, A y is ten.

19
00:00:51,851 --> 00:00:54,512
His second leg, B, is fifteen metres.

20
00:00:54,512 --> 00:00:56,986
Watch what happens as we turn leg B.

21
00:00:57,386 --> 00:00:59,752
The x parts stack on the x axis.

22
00:00:59,752 --> 00:01:02,117
The y parts stack on the y axis.

23
00:01:02,117 --> 00:01:04,422
R joins the start to the finish.

24
00:01:04,872 --> 00:01:05,898
Slow motion.

25
00:01:05,898 --> 00:01:08,776
Freeze at one hundred and twenty degrees.

26
00:01:08,776 --> 00:01:12,395
B x now points left, so
it takes away from R x.

27
00:01:12,895 --> 00:01:14,964
The graph shows the size of R.

28
00:01:14,964 --> 00:01:19,236
It is biggest at thirty degrees,
when both legs point the same way.

29
00:01:19,636 --> 00:01:22,335
Two legs or ten, the trick is the same.

30
00:01:22,335 --> 00:01:24,986
Add the x parts, then add the y parts.

31
00:01:25,586 --> 00:01:28,130
Let's write the rule, one step at a time.

32
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:29,433
Step one.

33
00:01:29,433 --> 00:01:30,979
Split each vector.

34
00:01:30,979 --> 00:01:33,780
A is A x i hat plus A y j hat.

35
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:36,580
B is B x i hat plus B y j hat.

36
00:01:37,330 --> 00:01:38,241
Step two.

37
00:01:38,241 --> 00:01:42,262
Add them, i hats with i
hats, j hats with j hats.

38
00:01:43,012 --> 00:01:44,204
Step three.

39
00:01:44,204 --> 00:01:49,684
So R x equals A x plus B x,
and R y equals A y plus B y.

40
00:01:50,434 --> 00:01:51,413
Step four.

41
00:01:51,413 --> 00:01:55,974
The size of R is the root of
R x squared plus R y squared.

42
00:01:56,724 --> 00:01:59,432
And tan theta equals R y over R x.

43
00:01:59,432 --> 00:02:02,564
Check the signs to pick
the right quadrant.

44
00:02:03,314 --> 00:02:04,427
Remember this.

45
00:02:04,427 --> 00:02:06,298
Add vectors part by part.

46
00:02:06,298 --> 00:02:08,024
x with x, y with y.

47
00:02:08,724 --> 00:02:10,907
Subtraction works the same way.

48
00:02:10,907 --> 00:02:12,030
Side by side.

49
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:14,352
On the left, A plus B.

50
00:02:14,352 --> 00:02:16,444
A is three i plus four j.

51
00:02:16,444 --> 00:02:18,144
B is two i minus j.

52
00:02:18,144 --> 00:02:19,375
Add the parts.

53
00:02:19,375 --> 00:02:21,064
Five i plus three j.

54
00:02:21,464 --> 00:02:23,508
On the right, A minus B.

55
00:02:23,508 --> 00:02:24,984
Subtract the parts.

56
00:02:24,984 --> 00:02:26,535
One i plus five j.

57
00:02:26,535 --> 00:02:28,525
Only the signs of B flip.

58
00:02:29,125 --> 00:02:30,423
Pause and think.

59
00:02:30,423 --> 00:02:33,591
Two vectors add up to
give R x equals zero.

60
00:02:33,591 --> 00:02:35,924
Must they be equal and opposite?

61
00:02:35,924 --> 00:02:37,275
Pause and decide.

62
00:02:40,475 --> 00:02:41,375
No!

63
00:02:40,971 --> 00:02:43,297
Only their x parts must cancel.

64
00:02:43,297 --> 00:02:48,488
Three i plus four j, and minus
three i plus two j, add up to six j.

65
00:02:48,988 --> 00:02:50,111
Now the signs.

66
00:02:50,111 --> 00:02:52,973
They tell you which
quadrant R points into.

67
00:02:53,323 --> 00:02:56,085
Quadrant one, x and y both positive.

68
00:02:56,085 --> 00:02:58,943
Quadrant two, x negative, y positive.

69
00:02:59,343 --> 00:03:01,524
Quadrant three, both negative.

70
00:03:01,524 --> 00:03:04,351
Quadrant four, x positive, y negative.

71
00:03:04,751 --> 00:03:05,871
Now you try.

72
00:03:05,871 --> 00:03:09,199
R x is minus four, and R y is plus three.

73
00:03:09,199 --> 00:03:11,656
Which quadrant does R point into?

74
00:03:11,656 --> 00:03:13,048
Pause and decide.

75
00:03:16,248 --> 00:03:17,702
The second quadrant!

76
00:03:17,702 --> 00:03:20,428
Negative x is left, positive y is up.

77
00:03:20,428 --> 00:03:22,950
Up and to the left is quadrant two.

78
00:03:23,450 --> 00:03:25,185
Now, one worked example.

79
00:03:25,535 --> 00:03:29,275
Aarav rides twenty metres at
thirty degrees north of east.

80
00:03:29,275 --> 00:03:31,170
Then five metres due north.

81
00:03:31,170 --> 00:03:33,055
Find his total displacement.

82
00:03:33,555 --> 00:03:34,498
First ride.

83
00:03:34,498 --> 00:03:38,240
A x is twenty cos thirty,
about seventeen point three.

84
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:41,151
A y is twenty sin thirty, which is ten.

85
00:03:41,901 --> 00:03:43,123
Second ride.

86
00:03:43,123 --> 00:03:44,497
B x is zero.

87
00:03:44,497 --> 00:03:45,870
B y is five.

88
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:47,934
Add the parts.

89
00:03:47,934 --> 00:03:50,328
R x is seventeen point three.

90
00:03:50,328 --> 00:03:51,770
R y is fifteen.

91
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:56,955
Size: the root of seventeen point
three squared plus fifteen squared.

92
00:03:56,955 --> 00:03:59,302
About twenty two point nine metres.

93
00:04:00,052 --> 00:04:04,009
Direction: tan theta is fifteen
over seventeen point three.

94
00:04:04,009 --> 00:04:06,658
About forty one degrees north of east.

95
00:04:07,158 --> 00:04:08,623
Now, the exam trap.

96
00:04:08,973 --> 00:04:13,905
Many students find the angle of minus
three i plus three j from tan theta

97
00:04:13,905 --> 00:04:17,207
equals minus one, and
write minus forty five.

98
00:04:17,557 --> 00:04:19,625
But that points down and right.

99
00:04:19,625 --> 00:04:24,076
Here A x is negative and A y positive,
so it is the second quadrant.

100
00:04:24,076 --> 00:04:26,048
The angle is one thirty five.

101
00:04:26,548 --> 00:04:28,153
Where is this asked?

102
00:04:28,153 --> 00:04:33,020
Mostly as a step inside bigger problems,
like resolving forces or finding

103
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:34,064
a resultant.

104
00:04:34,564 --> 00:04:35,897
Exam level now.

105
00:04:35,897 --> 00:04:38,235
A is six units along plus x.

106
00:04:38,235 --> 00:04:42,144
B is six root two units at
one thirty five degrees.

107
00:04:42,144 --> 00:04:44,595
C is four units along minus y.

108
00:04:44,595 --> 00:04:46,154
Find the resultant.

109
00:04:46,154 --> 00:04:47,544
Pause and solve.

110
00:04:52,944 --> 00:04:54,333
The answer is A.

111
00:04:54,333 --> 00:04:56,326
Two units, along plus y.

112
00:04:56,826 --> 00:05:00,986
R x is six, plus six root two
times cos one thirty five.

113
00:05:00,986 --> 00:05:02,732
That is six minus six.

114
00:05:02,732 --> 00:05:03,632
Zero.

115
00:05:03,825 --> 00:05:07,945
R y is six root two times sin
one thirty five, minus four.

116
00:05:07,945 --> 00:05:09,683
That is six minus four.

117
00:05:09,683 --> 00:05:10,583
Two.

118
00:05:10,704 --> 00:05:14,829
Taking cos one thirty five as
positive gives twelve point two.

119
00:05:14,829 --> 00:05:17,586
Dropping the minus sign on C gives ten.

120
00:05:17,586 --> 00:05:18,800
Both are traps.

121
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:20,759
Here is your recap.

122
00:05:20,759 --> 00:05:22,258
Screenshot this card.

123
00:05:25,458 --> 00:05:28,295
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

124
00:05:28,695 --> 00:05:29,595
One.

125
00:05:29,164 --> 00:05:32,431
To add two vectors, which
parts do you add together?

126
00:05:33,331 --> 00:05:34,231
Two.

127
00:05:33,919 --> 00:05:37,817
A is three i plus four
j, B is two i minus j.

128
00:05:37,817 --> 00:05:39,489
What is A minus B?

129
00:05:40,389 --> 00:05:41,289
Three.

130
00:05:40,991 --> 00:05:44,860
Why must you check the signs
before finding the angle of R?

131
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:51,055
Next time: velocity and acceleration
get x and y parts too, in motion in

132
00:05:51,055 --> 00:05:52,272
two dimensions.
